for more than two decades cops has  provided American families with  something to watch on Saturday nights  it's also opened a window into the work  of various local law enforcement  agencies the craziness we see on the air  is just what goes on in front of the  camera so here are just a few things  that have gone on behind the scenes  cops exists because of a writer strike  in researching his 1983 film cocaine  blues cops co-creator John Langley went  on ride-alongs to a couple of drug busts  his experience gave him the idea for  cops  Langley also worked on the Geraldo  Rivera hosted poorly received American  Vice the doping of a nation despite the  unfortunate association with Geraldo  Langley was able to come up with a  winning idea at the same time Hollywood  was suffering through a Writers Guild of  America strike and networks had a need  for unscripted programming this perfect  storm birthed cops and American  television has never been the same some  cities refused to allow filming because  police officers conduct serious work  cops film crews can't randomly show up  at any precinct and just start filming  after all having a camera crew following  you around all night can be annoying as  well as dangerous Langly fought through  this initial reluctance in order to get  his show on the air legend when we  started cops nobody wanted to be on top  including the cops I mean it was a very  bold idea the film crews need to get  permission and not all precincts comply  both Honolulu and Chicago have refused  to allow filming in their cities even  after multiple requests the reason for  the refusal is that police work is not  entertainment and cops trivializes  policing according to the Chicago Police  Department producers have been accused  of breaking the rules cops made an  entire episode out of the arrest of  Dalia Dippolito who was caught trying to  hire a hitman to murder her husband the  TV series was filming in the area when  the local PD sting operation went down  and cops got Dippolito signature on a  release form so they could air her  arrest dipa leo claims the release form  was misrepresented to her which the  police did not deny  the little lie didn't affect the jury  who still found her guilty she was  originally sentenced to 20 years in  prison but her conviction was reversed  in 2014  Dippolito is currently awaiting retrial  maybe cops can film a sequel episode  police accidentally killed a crew member  with all the danger of filming cops it's  not completely surprising that someone  has been killed during production in  August of 2014  police accidentally shot and killed  sound engineer Bryce Dion the incident  began when a pellet gun wielding suspect  pointed his weapon at a Wendy's employee  and the police opened fire police killed  the suspect along with Dion who was hit  by friendly fire while police claimed a  suspect opened fire on them the suspects  family claimed the officers were just  excited to be filmed and the tragic  incident resulted from them showing off  for the cameras Burt Lancaster was  involved before the folks at Fox felt  cops was just about ready to go they  decided it needed one more thing  starpower so in 1989 who was the biggest  star they could get Tom Cruise Michael  Keaton Patrick Swayze nope instead  Golden Age Hollywood handsome guy Burt  Lancaster alone his vocal talents to the  show the From Here to Eternity star  delivered the opening disclaimer for the  1989 pilot episode and that was it cops  is about real people and real crime it  was filmed entirely on location with the  men and women who work in law  enforcement there's no word on how much  it cost to hire Lancaster who hadn't had  a major role in almost a decade  but seeing us how they used his voice  just once let's hope for Fox's sake it  wasn't a lot of money it triumphed over  cancellation after over two decades as  one of Fox's go-to hits the network  pulled the plug on cops but fans of the  boys in blue didn't have to worry spike  TV soon picked up the show now cops can  be viewed alongside such dynamic fare as  ink master Bellator MMA and lip sync  battle  things have never looked better for  American law enforcement officers ends  heck America thanks for watching  subscribe to our YouTube channel to  watch more videos like the one you just  saw and leave us a comment to let us  know what you think of cops
 

